Based on Leandrohunter's unofficial NeoForge 1.21.1 port (fastsounds-0.5-neoforge-1.21.1).

Ported from FastSounds 0.6: non-blocking play (sounds start without the game
waiting on the sound thread), as a MixinExtras @WrapOperation instead of a
@Redirect so it stays compatible with other mods.

Changes from that port:
- Whitelist and critical-sound checks cached per sound id (no String allocation
  or list scanning per played sound / per eviction candidate).
- Removed the @Redirect on ChannelHandle.isStopped in tickNonPaused. On 1.21.1
  that call is a plain field read, so "staggered stopped" checks gave no gain and
  kept finished channels occupied for up to 5 extra ticks. Its config keys are
  kept as no-ops so existing configs still load.
- Evicting a sound now returns its OpenAL source to the pool immediately (queued
  on the sound thread ahead of the new sound's channel request). Before, evicted
  channels were only freed on the next tick, so in a burst the pool filled up and
  new sounds failed anyway ("Failed to create new sound handle") after farther
  sounds had already been cut. Already-evicted sounds no longer count toward
  maxConcurrentSounds, so later sounds don't evict more than needed.
- Distance culling and eviction measure from the camera (audio listener)
  instead of the player.
- Monotonic clock for cooldowns; floor() for the dedup grid on negative coords.
- Wider NeoForge range (21.1.x) and @Mod(dist = CLIENT).
Config file name, keys, defaults and ranges are unchanged.
